Z||000016||Archie||01-22-2001||10:35 AM||||HEY!!!, I have an idea for a meeting place.<P>I've been at Carlisle every year since the Kit Car Shows there started. Each year I'm in the same area, just West of the Red Building and just behind (South) of the Grandstand in the commercial area. I usually rent 2 spaces. I'm thinking it would be cool to rent a 3rd. space and set it up to be a Fiero Internet Gathering area. We can put a Guestbook out for Fiero people to sign in on as they arrive at the show. As they are signing in they can look at a board that will have messages posted by other Internet attendees dealing with meeting up with each other at various times & places throughout the weekend. We can have some stick on name tags available & if people use them, we will be able to identify each other during the event. Any & all of the various Internet Fiero lists/Forums/& members can post messages telling others where to meet or maybe which Hotel rooms will be party central etc. Kind of a hospitality center if you know what I mean.<P>Also, our Commercial & non Commercial Internet attendees that have Booths set-up to sell Fiero related items can post up messages telling where their booths are located.<P>What do you think?<P>Archie<p>[This message has been edited by Archie (edited 01-22-2001).]||||reg||4
