Z||000020||FieroLT1||01-22-2001||05:49 PM||||I think is an excellent idea. I haven't been to Carlisle since 1997 cause wheather has been so crapy. This year I'll be there for sure and would like to meet other listees too!<BR> <P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Archie:<BR><B>HEY!!!, I have an idea for a meeting place.<P>I've been at Carlisle every year since the Kit Car Shows there started. Each year I'm in the same area, just West of the Red Building and just behind (South) of the Grandstand in the commercial area. I usually rent 2 spaces. I'm thinking it would be cool to rent a 3rd. space and set it up to be a Fiero Internet Gathering area. We can put a Guestbook out for Fiero people to sign in on as they arrive at the show. As they are signing in they can look at a board that will have messages posted by other Internet attendees dealing with meeting up with each other at various times & places throughout the weekend. We can have some stick on name tags available & if people use them, we will be able to identify each other during the event. Any & all of the various Internet Fiero lists/Forums/& members can post messages telling others where to meet or maybe which Hotel rooms will be party central etc. Kind of a hospitality center if you know what I mean.<P>Also, our Commercial & non Commercial Internet attendees that have Booths set-up to sell Fiero related items can post up messages telling where their booths are located.<P>What do you think?<P>Archie<P>[This message has been edited by Archie (edited 01-22-2001).]</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><P>------------------<BR>Winston Ojeda<BR>88 Formula LT1<BR>Milwaukee, Wisconsin, USA<BR><A HREF="http://www.FieroLT1.com" TARGET=_blank>FieroLT1.com</A>||||reg||10
Z||000021||kslish||01-22-2001||07:33 PM||||I've attended for two years now....hopefully it'll be a nice sunny day like Carlisle '99 unlike the cold, wet weather of the 2000 event.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroMaster88:<BR><B>Yeah Lisa, <BR>Carlisle was fun last year, until a bunch of our group got lost!!!!  Maybe this year it will be better.  <BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Don't remind me. Also, don't forget the trip going there also. I still remember being on the shoulder of the PA Turnpike zip tying down a broken wiring harness connector to the coil of Craig's purple GT. If I cruise to Carlisle with you guys again this year, I'll be looking for cover if for some reason we don't make it there in time again for Lisa's car to be judged because all hell will break loose then.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> Just kidding Lisa. <P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR><BR><B>I have a question...how are we all gonna know each other???  We going to make signs to put in our windows or something??  Got to come up with something!<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>What happened to the vinyl decal idea?  I've already got my Fiero nametag ready from Bob Englert.<P>Ken S.<BR>'87 GT and '86 SC <A HREF="http://www.westpennfiero.org" TARGET=_blank>www.westpennfiero.org</A> ||||reg||10
